@startuml
title Sequence diagram: find a venue and request a booking
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' People work in the Web App, which calls the Backend API with their login token, so
' every call and its answer is two arrows: person <-> Web App, Web App <-> Backend API.
' Only the arrows to and from the Backend API and PostgreSQL are numbered, as in the
' draw.io and PDF versions.
' A notification is a record saved in PostgreSQL. Nothing is pushed to its recipient
' (no email, websocket or polling): the Web App fetches it later with
' GET /api/notifications, as the last section shows.

actor "Event\nCoordinator" as coordinator
actor "Venue\nStaff" as venue
participant "Web App\n(React)" as web
participant "Backend API" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== Find a venue and request a booking (the event must already be Approved) ==
coordinator -> web : Search venues
autonumber
web -> api : POST /api/venues/search
api --> web : The venues that match and are free
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show the venues

coordinator -> web : Check suitability
autonumber resume
web -> api : POST /api/venues/:id/suitability
api --> web : Suitable, or what is missing
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show the result

coordinator -> web : Request a venue booking
autonumber resume
web -> api : POST /api/venues/events/:reference/booking-requests
api -> db : Insert booking request (pending)
api -> db : Save notification:\nall Venue Staff
api --> web : The new request (pending)
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show the request

== Later, the Web App fetches Venue Staff's saved notifications (nothing is pushed) ==
venue -> web : Open notifications
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : A venue booking request awaits a decision
autonumber stop
web --> venue : Show notifications
@enduml
